Note: Phase 38 Plan 38-07 OSC-01 + OSC-02 loopback smoke — sends a
Note: single OSC message on 127.0.0.1:7777 to a listener registered
Note: on the same port + path, expecting the handler lambda to fire
Note: and print the received payload.
Note:
Note: AUTOMATED COVERAGE: the 19 xUnit Facts under
Note:   flow-lang.Tests/Integration/Phase38/Osc{TypeTagInference,RateLimit,Loopback,Bundle,BundleDepthCap}Tests.cs
Note: pin every Plan 38-06 contract — type-tag inference, sample-and-hold
Note: rate limit, UDP loopback round-trip preserves payload within 2 s
Note: (bounded per Pitfall #10 anti-flake), bundle dispatch + depth-cap
Note: clamp at 8 with WarnOnce advisory. They all pass deterministically.
Note:
Note: MANUAL SMOKE (composer host):
Note:   dotnet run --project flow-interpreter tests/test_live_osc_controller.flow
Note: Expected: prints "fader=0.5" then PASS sentinel; the (oscStop h)
Note: tears down the receive loop.

use "@std"
use "@osc"

Note: Spawn the receive loop on 127.0.0.1:7777 listening for "/fader/1".
Note: Returns an OscHandle reference-identity value per D-38-16.
OscHandle h = (oscListen 7777 "/fader/1" (fn Double v => (print (concat "fader=" (str v)))))

Note: Round-trip a single Double payload. oscSend infers ,d per D-38-13
Note: (charitable smallest-tag-that-fits) and emits across the loopback
Note: interface; the listener's handler fires and prints "fader=0.5".
(oscSend "127.0.0.1" 7777 "/fader/1" 0.5)

Note: Cancel the listener's CancellationTokenSource + dispose the
Note: receiver per Pitfall #5 workaround (Cts.Cancel alone can't
Note: interrupt the blocked Receive() syscall).
(oscStop h)

(print "PASS: OSC loopback round-trip")
